<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charlotte Harbor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charlotte Harbor is a large estuary on the Gulf coast of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, fed by the Peace and Myakka rivers. Its rich fisheries supported the Calusa, whose shell-mound towns lined its shores and islands, such as Pineland. Spanish expeditions, including those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-ponce-de-leon">Juan Ponce de León</a>, reached the area in the early 16th century.</p></div>
